WEBVTT

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:04.980
Come on, we can handle
a long-distance thing.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.360
I'm totally gonna go to a university
 in Kyoto for you, Aoi.

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.310
And I'll keep an eye out so he doesn't cheat.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:13.460
You rest easy and go to Kyoto, okay?

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:16.870
Thanks, Sanae, Katsumi.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:25.770
<i>Sorry. I can't take this anymore.</i>

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:28.730
Why?

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.300
Katsumi! Sanae!

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.520
That dream again?

00:00:57.510 --> 00:01:03.100
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:19.240
Episode 4

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:19.240
"After the Festival"

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:29.000
The Gion Festival, huh?

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:35.570
<i>Don't get depressed before work.</i>

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:41.720
Hello!

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:43.970
Ah, Aoi-chan! Hello there.

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:46.470
Akihito-san? What are you doing here?

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:49.250
He came to see Kiyotaka-chan.

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:51.810
Can ya believe it? He's an actor!

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.410
And handsome to boot!

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:55.690
Why, thank you.

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:58.490
I came to give him a more 
proper thank you for before.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.010
Oh, I see...

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:02.870
Um, where <i>is</i> Holmes-san?

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.120
I was preparing coffee.

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:10.730
Akihito-san brought us some 
Ryokujuan Shimizu konpeito.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.650
I'll make your café au lait next, Aoi-san.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.760
Is something the matter?

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.390
Oh, n-no...

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:22.020
I was just a little surprised 
to see you in a yukata.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:24.890
It's on the owner's orders.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:28.520
I have to wear a yukata in-store 
until the Gion Festival is over.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.220
Speakin' of which, the owner
asked me to do something, too.

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:35.520
He wanted me to to get some yukatas 
together for his charmin' part-timer.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:39.400
It's from my shop, but it's got fasteners, 
so you can put it on all by yourself.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:41.800
S-Sure...

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.720
Why, don't you look lovely?

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:51.300
Totally cute, Aoi-chan!

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:58.670
You look truly charming. 
It suits you very well.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:01.170
Thank you...

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:03.930
And ya got the "migi-mae" closure right, too.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:08.680
I've... worn one before, 
so putting it on this way felt right...

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:10.310
You did well.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:14.190
"Migi-mae" means "right-front," because
the right side goes on the inside.

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:17.080
Put even more simply,

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:20.990
if a man holding you from behind 
can slip his right hand easily inside,

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:24.070
you did it right.

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:26.570
Yukatas are so sensual, aren't they?

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:28.420
<i>H-He's so close!</i>

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:30.540
Excuse me.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:33.460
Please refrain from sexual harassment 
in our place of business.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:36.520
Fine, I get it already!

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:40.460
Sheesh, Holmes-kun. 
You're totally the jealous type...

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:41.890
Jealous?

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:44.470
You're dating, aren't you?

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:46.210
N-No way!

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:49.350
She's just a student we happen to employ.

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:52.250
I see.

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:56.730
Then I guess I came at the right time, 
since I got to see Aoi-chan in a yukata.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:02.740
Akihito-san, you've done what you 
came for, so you're free to leave now.

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:05.240
You <i>are</i> mad.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:10.990
Yes, with an anger specially reserved for 
arrogant, overbearing playboys like you.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:13.860
What the heck?

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:22.370
I'll have your other yukatas 
ready by Yoi Yoi Yama.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:25.260
I'll be in the area for a while, 
so I might come to hang out again.

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:32.010
What's "Yoi Yoi Yama"?

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:35.270
It's an evening festival held two 
nights before the Gion Festival.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:39.220
The Gion Festival was first 
held over a thousand years ago.

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:42.220
They send floats called 
"yamaboko" down the streets

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:45.160
to keep the city safe from 
disaster and to purify it.

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:48.530
You could say it's the most famous 
of Kyoto's three great festivals.

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:51.750
Two nights from now, at the 
Yoi Yoi Yama festival on the 15th,

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:56.530
they'll line up the illuminated yamaboko 
along the avenue. It's very beautiful.

00:05:57.570 --> 00:06:00.540
I see... And that's on the 15th?

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:02.290
Aoi-san?

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:07.640
You've seemed a bit listless 
the entire time you've been here.

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:09.180
Is there something on your mind?

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:12.820
<i>Of course Holmes-san would notice...</i>

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:17.370
Actually, um...

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:19.770
Welcome.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:29.060
Izumi?

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:32.660
Hello there, Kiyotaka-kun.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:35.280
It's been quite a long time, Izumi-san.

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:37.280
I'm pleased to see that you're well.

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:40.170
Aw, you don't gotta be so formal...

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:41.920
I heard about your marriage.

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:43.920
You have my congratulations.

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:45.480
<i>Marriage?!</i>

00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:51.890
It seems she's going to marry that 
arrogant and overbearing Osakan.

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:55.260
<i>Could she be...?</i>

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:58.150
He asked me today

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:02.770
if I could have a dish my aunt gave 
us for our wedding appraised

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.450
to see how much it was worth.

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:07.030
Very well.

00:07:08.890 --> 00:07:11.660
Allow me to take a look, then.

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:17.660
It's a Royal Copenhagen?

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:19.500
Is it really?

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:23.670
All I know of Copenhagen 
is the Christmas Plates...

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:25.920
That's fair.

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:27.880
The Christmas Plates are so popular,

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.330
they're the primary association most 
people have with Royal Copenhagen.

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:34.640
They've been putting them 
out since 1908, after all.

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:38.770
But this one ain't blue... 
So what's it really?

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:39.850
It's true...

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:46.020
The hand-painted cobalt blue designs, 
strongly influenced by Japan's Imari ware,

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:48.780
are one of Royal Copenhagen's trademarks.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:52.280
But they also create many 
pieces that lack that feature.

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:55.780
This is part of a series produced over
sixty years ago,

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:59.760
depicting scenery from all over Europe.

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:01.420
As for its worth... Let me see...

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:04.540
I would say about 20,000 or 30,000 yen.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.800
I see. That's awful good to hear.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:11.050
Kiyotaka-kun, you're just so amazin'.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:14.300
I heard rumors you got into Kyoto 
University's graduate program, too.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:17.550
That's hardly related... 
This is just my family business.

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:23.310
The truth is... all <i>he</i> knew about 
Copenhagen was the cobalt blue stuff.

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:26.310
"It's gotta be a fake," he said.

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:30.820
I told him my aunt wasn't that 
kinda person, but he kept insistin'...

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:32.880
That sounds quite troubling.

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:36.310
I'm always thinkin' about dumpin' him!

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:40.870
He cheated on me a bunch 
while we were datin'...

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:43.150
But each time, he'd worm his way out of it.

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:45.580
When I'd start talkin' about 
how we should break up,

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:48.260
he'd start bawlin' and sayin' he was sorry.

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:53.090
We ended up married and all, but...

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:57.860
The more time goes by, the more I start 
thinkin', "Is this really the guy for me?"

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:03.980
And when he brought up the Copenhagen thing, 
your face immediately popped into my head...

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:08.170
Kiyotaka-kun, do you still like waka poetry?

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:09.480
Well, yes...

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:11.980
<i>Why waka poetry?</i>

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:14.100
I'd like ya to have a look at this, too.

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:18.490
I'll come to get it two days 
from now, during Yoi Yoi Yama.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:19.990
You want me to look at it by then?

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:23.500
Yeah. I made it on a mountain in Shiga.

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:25.490
A mountain in Shiga?

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:31.000
I'm sorry. You made that 
coffee for me, but...

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:31.940
It's fine.

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:34.310
A tea bowl?

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:36.260
With... a leaf pattern?

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:38.580
Yes. Japanese mugwort.

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:40.780
Does that have some kind of meaning?

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:42.510
I'm not sure...

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:48.150
In the poems of the Hyakunin Isshu, 
it's also known as "sashimo grass."

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:52.900
Sashimo grass... Holmes-san, 
you really do like waka, then?

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:54.870
Well, it's not my favorite...

00:09:55.350 --> 00:09:58.950
But waka was what first brought us together.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.910
In the fall of my second year of 
high school, during a school event,

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:05.800
we went to Tofukuji Temple, which is
 famous for its autumn colors.

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:11.330
Reminds you of that poem, don't it?

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:15.180
"Not even the gods in their boundless 
multitudes have seen such a sight."

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:17.970
Um, the last verse was...

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:20.760
"Ah, the Tatsuta River, crimson-washed 
with autumn leaves!"

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:27.020
She said that that was when she 
first developed feelings for me.

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:28.840
I see...

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:33.270
<i>If someone like him recited that 
last verse to me, I'd fall pretty hard, too.</i>

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:37.530
Anyway, I believe you were in the 
middle of telling me something.

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:39.430
Oh, um...

00:10:40.650 --> 00:10:43.560
My friends from school back in Saitama...

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:47.040
They're coming to see 
the Gion Festival for a school trip.

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:54.040
And a girl from my old circle emailed me
 asking to meet up at their hotel.

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:57.840
But my former best friend is in that group...

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:00.930
And I'm afraid I might run 
into my old boyfriend, too...

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:06.430
But I do want to see the others, 
so I told her I'd go.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:08.020
I see.

00:11:08.450 --> 00:11:11.940
It's still bothering you, huh?

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:16.020
If they're going to come to you, 
that might be for the best.

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:18.690
I suppose... that's true.

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:21.100
When are you going to see them?

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:25.760
The 15th... So on Yoi Yoi Yama.
 At 7:30 that night.

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:28.830
And you're working until 
7:00 that night, aren't you?

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:33.080
Yes. It's perfect timing, I'll admit...

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:35.170
Try not to let it weigh on you so heavily.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:37.090
"The worry is worse than 
the labor," as they say,

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:38.200
Aoi-san.

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:44.490
Holmes-san...

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:50.940
<i>Two days from now...</i>

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:55.150
<i>What will Holmes-san do after 
examining that tea bowl?</i>

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:57.830
<i>And... what should I do?</i>

00:12:02.730 --> 00:12:04.360
Oh, how fine.

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:06.020
It suits you so well.

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:07.370
Thank you very much.

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:09.390
Japanese clothing is so nice.

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:11.750
And you really have wonderful taste, Mieko-san.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:14.160
Well, I do run a clothing store.

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:17.880
But it was Kiyotaka-chan 
who chose that yutaka.

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:20.920
He's got awful fine judgment.

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:23.130
And he knows you inside and out!

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:24.970
Holmes-san picked it?

00:12:29.730 --> 00:12:32.490
<i>His yutaka looks great on him, too...</i>

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:34.320
<i>That's a Kyoto boy for you!</i>

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:36.790
It sounds as if things are 
getting lively outside.

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:38.360
Y-Yeah.

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:40.400
Well, that's the Gion Festival for you!

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:43.220
It's almost time for Yoi Yoi Yama.

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:46.410
You're going to see your 
friends tonight, aren't you?

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:48.230
Y-Yes...

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:52.660
And... Izumi-san is coming by today too, right?

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:53.930
I believe so.

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:55.420
She did say it would be today.

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:57.110
D-Did she?

00:12:57.110 --> 00:12:57.780
Yes.

00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:00.490
Welcome.

00:13:00.490 --> 00:13:01.420
W-Welcome!

00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:10.500
Aoi-san.

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:13.300
Will you make it in time?

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:18.440
Oh, yeah. Their hotel is nearby, 
so as long as I leave by 7:20...

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:19.950
I see.

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:22.440
I have to deliver something 
to the association,

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:25.200
so would you mind watching the 
shop for a few minutes?

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:26.170
Okay.

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:33.590
Izumi-san isn't here yet...

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:38.710
<i>What does that mugwort mean?</i>

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:44.260
In the poems of the Hyakunin Isshu, 
it's also known as "sashimo grass."

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:47.050
I made it on a mountain in Shiga.

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:50.950
<i>Mt. Ibuki... Mt. Shirakuradake...</i>

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:54.270
<i>The map's not really helping...</i>

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:55.930
<i>What about the Hyakunin Isshu?</i>

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:59.670
"Like life-giving dew to the parched 
sasemo grass was your oath to me.

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:01.970
Yet the autumn comes and passes, 
and your oath is unfulfilled."

00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:02.940
That's not it...

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:06.440
"Ah, to say it— No; but surely I 
cannot hide the fire that blazes

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:09.640
so high and hot, 
like the sashimo grass of Ibuki."

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:12.330
Ibuki. That's a mountain in Shiga...

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:13.700
This must be it.

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:15.950
And it means... um...

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:22.710
I'm sorry. That took longer than I thought.

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:23.780
That's okay.

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:26.930
Nobody came, anyway. It was fine.

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:30.840
Well, I'd better go get changed...

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:32.060
Aoi-san.

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:35.970
Since it's the Gion Festival, 
why don't you just go in your yukata?

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:39.590
Your friends might be wearing yukatas, too.

00:14:39.590 --> 00:14:42.360
And it really does suit you.

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:45.260
Th-That's true.

00:14:45.260 --> 00:14:48.410
As long as I have it on, 
I might as well wear it there.

00:14:50.310 --> 00:14:51.590
Kiyotaka-kun.

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:53.800
Welcome.

00:14:53.800 --> 00:14:55.240
Please, have a seat.

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:56.660
Much obliged!

00:14:58.890 --> 00:15:02.130
<i>Holmes-san would have 
known it from the start.</i>

00:15:02.530 --> 00:15:03.950
<i>The meaning of the poem...</i>

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:06.880
<i>The feelings she was conveying 
with that tea bowl...</i>

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:11.840
<i>"Although I love you dearly, I cannot say it.</i>

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:19.390
<i>Can't you see that my love for you burns 
like the sashimo grass on Mt. Ibuki?"</i>

00:15:19.880 --> 00:15:23.560
<i>What will Holmes-san do after 
seeing the girl he used to love?</i>

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:25.640
This way!

00:15:26.090 --> 00:15:27.000
Hurry!

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:32.410
<i>And if I run into the man I used to love 
with my best friend... What will I do?</i>

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:35.120
<i>What... should I...</i>

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:36.530
Hey, it's Aoi!

00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:42.540
G-Guys!

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.650
You look great, Aoi!

00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:47.250
You look majorly cute in a yukata, too!

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.940
I'm so glad. You're all just the same...

00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:51.800
I'm glad I came.

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:57.310
Actually, Aoi... Sanae and Katsumi 
really need to talk to you!

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:02.290
Sorry, Aoi.

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:03.560
We're sorry!

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:08.580
You probably heard through 
the grapevine already...

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:11.200
But we're dating now.

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:13.230
It happened after you left.

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:16.320
Katsumi and I were both so lonely...

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:20.830
We started going to karaoke and stuff 
to help get our minds off it...

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:22.210
It's all my fault.

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:23.700
No, it's my fault!

00:16:23.700 --> 00:16:26.330
I started to develop feelings for Katsumi...

00:16:26.640 --> 00:16:28.840
I started wanting to spend 
all my time with Sanae...

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:30.590
I'm really sorry!

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:32.840
<i>What?</i>

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:34.390
Forgive them, okay?

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:36.390
They're trying to make it right.

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:38.100
That's why we invited you here.

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:44.350
<i>I get it... They didn't actually want to see me.</i>

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:49.360
<i>I don't have any friends who 
really care about me anymore.</i>

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:52.360
Hey... it's fine.

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:57.620
We drifted apart because I moved away.

00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:01.250
It's a little hard to accept my 
boyfriend and best friend dating,

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:03.640
but it's not like you can 
help who you fall for.

00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:07.130
Don't worry about me. 
Take care of each other, okay?

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:09.480
Thank you, Aoi...

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:12.270
Aoi, you're so awesome!

00:17:12.270 --> 00:17:13.050
Totally cool!

00:17:13.520 --> 00:17:16.890
Hey, now that we're all friends again, 
let's go around the festival together!

00:17:17.230 --> 00:17:19.390
<i>Stop it! Please!</i>

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:20.690
Aoi-san?

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:24.770
Who's that? He's hot!

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:27.510
You know him, Aoi? Is he in college?

00:17:27.510 --> 00:17:28.770
Y-Yeah...

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:30.690
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:32.970
My name is Yagashira Kiyotaka.

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:37.410
I am a student of language and 
literature at Kyoto University.

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:40.110
Kyoto University?! Wow!

00:17:40.110 --> 00:17:42.040
Have you finished your discussion?

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:44.540
Y-Yes...

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:47.650
Then let us see the festival together.

00:17:49.050 --> 00:17:50.670
O-Okay. Sure thing...

00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:52.210
Hey, Aoi!

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:53.330
What the hell?

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:56.930
The minute I'm not around, you start 
dating some Kyoto University guy?!

00:17:58.180 --> 00:17:59.680
Katsumi! What's wrong with you?!

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:06.430
Hey, Sanae! Wait a minute!

00:18:06.430 --> 00:18:07.820
That's not how I meant it!

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:08.690
Aoi-san?

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:10.440
R-Right...

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:15.690
You surprised me, Holmes-san.

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:17.230
Did you come to find me?

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:19.480
Well, I was concerned...

00:18:19.480 --> 00:18:22.830
I had a feeling you were crying.

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:27.080
You're as amazing as ever, Holmes-san.

00:18:28.020 --> 00:18:30.030
I'd reached my limit.

00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:32.490
They apologized without caring how I felt.

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:35.240
All my friends took their side.

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:40.340
But I gave them my blessing anyway.

00:18:40.740 --> 00:18:43.510
"It's not for them. It's for me."

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:47.140
That's what I told myself, 
but I guess I couldn't take it.

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:49.740
At least it's over with now.

00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:55.110
You worried about me, you came 
to help me, you saved me...

00:18:55.850 --> 00:18:58.650
I really can't thank you enough.

00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:01.140
You don't gotta force yourself to smile.

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:02.910
What they did was wrong.

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:08.970
If they'd really felt bad and 
wanted to say they were sorry,

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:12.130
why'd they need to hide behind their friends?

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:14.420
I never heard of somethin' so underhanded.

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:16.440
Holmes-san...

00:19:20.020 --> 00:19:22.930
You've been through a lot, Aoi-san.

00:19:29.170 --> 00:19:31.120
You go on and cry all you like.

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:33.940
You did good today, Aoi-san.

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:43.220
Here you are.

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:44.730
Thank you very much.

00:19:47.060 --> 00:19:51.710
Holmes-san, did you pick up on the message 
Izumi-san was conveying with the tea bowl?

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:54.210
Yes... Wait, did you as well?

00:19:56.290 --> 00:20:00.490
"Ah, to say it— No; but surely I 
cannot hide the fire that blazes..."

00:20:00.490 --> 00:20:03.460
"...so high and hot, 
like the sashimo grass of Ibuki."

00:20:04.490 --> 00:20:06.090
I'm surprised.

00:20:06.090 --> 00:20:07.910
I'm impressed that you realized it.

00:20:07.910 --> 00:20:09.720
Oh, well... you know.

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:14.730
I had a feeling she wanted a 
reply poem, so I gave her one.

00:20:14.730 --> 00:20:15.950
Reply poem?

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:18.980
Yes. I wrote a little parody 
of Suo no Naishi's poem.

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:22.780
"For a passing whim as brief as a 
summer dream, to rest on your arm...

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:25.490
What worth has such a pillow, 
if it should smother my name?"

00:20:26.920 --> 00:20:31.620
"To indulge this passing fancy of yours, 
which will last as long as a summer's dream,

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:35.290
is not worth having people spread 
rumors about our relationship."

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:37.290
That's what it meant.

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:40.300
<i>Wow... That's Kyoto boys for you.</i>

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:44.300
You're wrong, Aoi-san. 
The saying is "Kyoto men."

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:51.050
The lines in the tea bowl that she made 
for me showed calculation and hesitation.

00:20:51.620 --> 00:20:56.810
It communicated that her pursuit of 
me was motivated by mere escapism.

00:20:56.810 --> 00:21:02.320
Art will always reveal the 
true feelings of its creator.

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:04.840
I told her that if she was 
feeling that uncertain,

00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:07.240
she should talk it out properly 
with him and her parents,

00:21:07.240 --> 00:21:10.580
or she may regret it all her life.

00:21:10.580 --> 00:21:13.480
She then stormed out, sulking.

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:17.460
Oh, really?

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:21.100
<i>Huh?</i>

00:21:21.100 --> 00:21:23.340
Aoi-san? Is something the matter?

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:27.530
Oh, n-no! It's nothing...

00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:28.610
I mean it...

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:32.020
It really is nothing!

00:21:32.630 --> 00:21:36.270
Aoi-san, your café au lait 
appears to have gotten cold.

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:37.890
Shall I make you a new one?

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:40.920
P-Please do...

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:50.660
<i>Why did hearing that story 
make me feel so relieved?</i>

00:21:57.560 --> 00:22:04.530
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:51.500
Next Episode

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:51.500
"The Lost Dragon"

00:23:37.930 --> 00:23:41.730
Holmes-san! Where did you 
go after you left me behind?

00:23:41.730 --> 00:23:44.660
I went to see someone I would 
prefer to have avoided.

00:23:45.330 --> 00:23:47.820
Next time: "The Lost Dragon."

00:23:47.820 --> 00:23:49.990
Holmes-san, you really are nasty.
